infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Template parser vs codegen: when the string needs parsing, generate it
  desc Same end-to-end string safety — but a recursive type parser is one no debugger can step through
  compares
    - label Template literal parser
      children
        - label When the string IS the contract
          desc Router :id, typed i18n key, SQL-ish DSL — the format is the API
        - label Zero-runtime end-to-end safety
          desc :id checked against req.params, no duplicated declaration
        - label Cross product caps out
          desc 50x50x50 = 125,000 past the ~100k union cap; 26^4 ~ 457,000 errors or OOMs
        - label Recursion wall ~50 deep
          desc Past it, silently resolves to string — every call site loses its check
    - label Codegen / build step
      children
        - label When the string needs PARSING
          desc A non-trivial grammar at the type level is the signal to switch
        - label Flat named types
          desc Generated route-map union is greppable and hover-clean
        - label Compiles instantly
          desc No instantiation-depth limit, no millions-count blowup, no editor lag
        - label A parser you can step through
          desc Unlike a recursive template that no debugger can enter
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
